gagement with students. Lecturers are hired on an as-needed basis across a range of instructional areas, including applied music, class piano, ensembles, jazz studies, music education, music history and literature, music technology, music theory, and general education courses for non-majors. Tenure Track Faculty -  Latin American Music Sacramento April 03, 2026 Open Until Filled The School of Music at Sacramento State seeks a highly skilled and inspiring musician/educator for a full-time, tenure-track position in Latin American Music beginning in January 2027. This position reflects the University’s commitment to inclusive excellence, culturally sustaining pedagogy, and the musical traditions that reflect and serve our large Latinx/é and Hispanic student population. Salary will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. 2026-27 AY Lecturer Pool - Communication Studies Sacramento April 03, 2026 Open Until Filled The Department of Communication Studies seeks part-time instructors to teach courses in communication, public relations, journalism, and film. The department offers a variety of courses that focus on understanding the communication process and developing skills to communicate effectively. Areas include intercultural, interpersonal, group, and organizational communication, rhetorical theory and criticism, public relations, mediated communication, journalism, and film. 2026-27 AY Lecturer & Clinical Pool - School of Nursing Sacramento April 03, 2026 Open Until Filled The School of Nursing is seeking candidates for our part-time lecturer/clinical pool to teach clinical and skills in the undergraduate prelicensure program. We occasionally have the need for part-time lecturers in the RN-BSN, MSN, and School Nurse programs. Of particular interest are for those interested in clinical teaching in the areas of mental health, school nursing, and community health. Teaching in the School Nursing program can be year-round as courses are also held in summer. 2026-